MCP Server: A new Model Context Protocol (MCP) server is now available as an optional, separately deployed component of Gentics Mesh Enterprise. It exposes published Gentics Mesh content to AI agents and LLM-based tools through a small set of well-defined MCP tools (listing projects and schemas, loading nodes by UUID or webroot path, searching nodes and running GraphQL queries), so language models never talk to the Gentics Mesh API directly. Access is restricted by a policy layer (project and language allowlists), protected by rate limiting, bulkheads and a circuit breaker, and authenticated with a Bearer token in HTTP mode. The server is shipped as its own container image.
See "MCP Server":https://www.gentics.com/mesh/docs/mcp-server/ in the documentation for details.
